WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.458
PRIYANKA VERGADIA:
This week, we're

00:00:01.458 --> 00:00:03.440
talking about
migrating, streaming,

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:07.070
and generating insights
with your data on BigQuery.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:10.370
I'm Priyanka, and welcome to
"This Week in Cloud," where

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:13.640
we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.680
Traditional data
warehouses can be

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.410
expensive and
difficult to maintain

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:23.630
as data rapidly increases in
volume, velocity, and variety.

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.870
We know that businesses are
turning to BigQuery to keep up,

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.510
so we've put together
a quick guide on how

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.880
to start your migration plan.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.640
Get prepared by creating
a migration plan

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.140
and then going through the full
data warehouse migration guide.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.540
Storing data in
cloud storage helps

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:44.900
you not only keep your
files accessible and secure

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:49.100
but also gets them ready
for real time analysis.

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.410
By using Cloud
Functions, you can

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:54.710
run code every time
a file is uploaded

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.440
and stream the
data into BigQuery.

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:01.820
Follow along and try it out for
yourself in the solution guide.

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.640
Now that you can move
more data to BigQuery,

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.910
we're also making it easier
to work with your data

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:11.390
using persistent User
Defined Functions.

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.960
Felipe has another
great post detailing out

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:19.160
how to create and share UDF's
across your organization.

00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:21.950
Check out the details
to create your own

00:01:21.950 --> 00:01:25.400
or use the ones that
Felipe has shared.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.340
Looking for some more guided
practice with BigQuery?

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.800
We'll unroll in From
Data to Insights

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.010
with GCP specialization
on Coursera.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.910
You learn how to query and
process petabytes of data

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.440
on BigQuery.

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:42.590
It's got interactive
scenarios and hands-on labs

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.890
to give you meaningful practice
at skills that have never

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.290
been more relevant.

00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:49.400
Enroll today.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:52.130
If you want to read more
about this announcement

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:55.380
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.210
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.610
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:02.290
We'll see you in the cloud.

